# Ptolemy's second theorem, general convex cyclic quadrilateral — AC·(AB·BC + CD·DA) = BD·(AB·AD + BC·CD); D is the second meet of the B-median with the circumcircle, so ABCD is convex and not a trapezoid (source: Ptolemy, Almagest)
A B C = triangle
M = midpoint(A, C)
D = meet(line(B, M), circumcircle(A, B, C))
prove dist(A, C) * (dist(A, B) * dist(B, C) + dist(C, D) * dist(D, A)) = dist(B, D) * (dist(A, B) * dist(A, D) + dist(B, C) * dist(C, D))
